1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,400
Social Links: your LinkedIn, GitHub and every other profile link, one right-click away.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,600
Every application asks for the same profile links.

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:15,500
Right-click in the box › Social links › LinkedIn › Paste here.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:20,600
Same for GitHub, or any link you've saved.

5
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:26,000
Or open any saved link in a new tab.

6
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:30,900
No mouse needed: type sl, a space and a name in the address bar.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,500
sl c github copies the link instead.

8
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:41,000
Right-click a profile link › + Add this link. Platform and username detected.

9
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,500
Saved: X now shows ✎ Edit instead of + Add.

10
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,300
Everything lives behind the toolbar button.

11
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,300
+ means not added yet. ✎ means saved: click it to edit.

12
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,200
Other link suggests 35 sites as you type: Kaggle, Hugging Face, Devpost…

13
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,900
Pick one and type just your username.

14
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:59,000
Saved as Kaggle, ready in the menu and the address bar.

15
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:05,500
★ marks your main links. Only those go on the share card.

16
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:11,500
Share card: one scan saves your ★ main links as a contact. vCard too.

17
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:17,000
Separate Work and Personal profiles. Switch here or from the menu.

18
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:22,200
Back up to a file. Restore with a preview, then merge or replace.

19
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:28,700
Private by design: only types into a page when you choose Paste, never reads it. No tracking, no network requests.

20
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:35,000
Social Links is free and open source: github.com/mukeshkbj/SocialLinks
